**Read:** [Atomic layer deposition — surface chemistry and evidence](../sources/Atomic-Layer-Deposition-Chemistry-and-Evidence.lingua#r_43RJYA2HWF0DWTRB766G062RHV), the complete review and primary gravimetric study. Revisit surface chemistry, kinetics and gas transport.

Sequential precursor exposures and separation steps can produce self-terminating surface reactions. Growth per cycle need not equal a crystallographic monolayer: reactive sites, ligands, steric constraints, nucleation and surface state matter. A flat growth-versus-dose region on one specimen does not prove identical saturation throughout a deep porous structure.

**Work:** Draw the material and surface-site account for one documented cycle. Compare mass uptake, composition, thickness and accessible surface area before inferring a unique mechanism. Vary dose, purge, temperature and cycle count in the published evidence and identify signs of condensation, decomposition or incomplete penetration. Derive a transport/reaction scaling for a recessed feature and propose independent measurements of coverage and impurity content. Keep an ideal self-limiting reaction distinct from the performance of the complete deposition apparatus.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
